  "requested_focus": "Review and preserve the completed broadcast experiment d65529a2: FP16 D126 improved 1.0996x, FP32 D254 regressed 6.07%, geomean only1.001942x. Do not broadly promote it or run a platform trial of that mixed result. Target a larger general unaligned dataflow benefit through pipeline overlap, keeping frequency/trig and original 4Mul+Sub/Add arithmetic unchanged.\n\nUse the official 48.78 archived source817f8364 as parent, not canonical V9. First write a capacity/liveness/queue-dependency model, referring to existing AlignedRotary and DirectFloatRotary protocols. Candidate design: FP16 compact broadcast plus two input/two output slots fits approximately36*capacity bytes plus trig/frequency storage; no tile change is necessary at capacity4096. For FP32, direct input/output queue computation can remove LoadFp32/StoreFp32 UB copies and release work space. Retaining dense coefficients plus a temporary uses approximately3*capacity FP32 work elements; with four queue slots the total is about44*capacity bytes plus frequency storage (~180KiB at capacity4096), under188KiB. Account separately for small-head trig scratch (angle/q/temp), frequency fallback allocations and padding; these are design estimates to verify, not permission to overallocate.\n\nPerform causal variants: first a FP32 queue-direct copy-removal variant with original queue depths/synchronization; then add input/output double buffering and next-job prefetch with proven TQue dependencies. FP16 may use the measured compact-broadcast path as an isolated intermediate, but retain the original FP32 behavior until its own variant is validated. Compare each intermediate to its proper parent and compare the final combined source to817f8364. Do not mix in new math, DMA strategy, tiling, hidden-case routing or extra kernels. If the proposed model is wrong, report and revise from evidence rather than mechanically implementing it.\n\nFor steady-state overlap remove per-job PIPE_ALL only where ownership/events prove safety; keep the final drain. Position0 must preserve input bits incl NaN/Inf/signed0; use a proven input-to-output queue copy protocol rather than an unsafe direct VECIN-to-MTE3 path. Tail groups, queued DMA completion before slot reuse, and empty/last-job prefetch need explicit review. Keep within the existing original-template C++14/SDK dav-2201 interface; no package installation, new third-party libraries, generated helper files or build/link changes.\n\nValidate all source-bound original precision/guard/identity/nonfinite/launch gates and bitwise equivalence to817f8364 across the prior1625 cases plus long-reuse/pipeline tails. Preserve the inherited frozen amplitude max32 failure and report parent/candidate classifications separately; do not change the golden or thresholds, exclude the failure, or claim universal correctness. Require no new output differences. Use serial single-card task-submit max-time60 throughout; CPU preparation/compilation outside reservations. Native paired ABBA+BAAB and fixed33 controls decide benefit; PMU replay only diagnoses. At most two implementation intermediates and one final archived experimental candidate in this request. Archive patches/sources, hashes, genuine validation, timing/PMU, rejected paths and decision, commit/push, then stop for coordinator review. Do not publish production ready/latest or submit to the platform yourself. The Mac can perform one genuine platform trial of a substantially faster reviewed candidate under the user's authorization."
